  "summary_insights": [
    "FY26 revenue growth is marginal at 1.9%, constrained by regulatory approval delays in the UK building sector which have deferred project timelines.",
    "Gross margin compressed from 37.8% to 35.2% in FY26, driven by a 6.3% increase in cost of sales that outpaced turnover growth.",
    "Operating expenses rose significantly by 17.5% in FY26 due to temporary operational investments in systems and headcount to support future scaling.",
    "Net profit is forecast to decline by 40.3% in FY26, reflecting the combined impact of margin compression and elevated overhead investment.",
    "Management forecasts a strong recovery from FY27 onwards, with revenue projected to reach £22.9m and EBITDA margins expanding to 15.4% by FY28.",
    "The business maintains a substantial pipeline of £83m in quoted work, suggesting that current revenue stagnation is a timing issue rather than a demand deficit.",
    "Interest coverage remains exceptionally high, indicating that the company has very low financial risk and significant headroom on debt service."
  ],
